<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">King Fuchu of Chu</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 227–223 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a> · Also known as Xiong Fuchu</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">King Fuchu was the last king of the State of Chu, reigning from 227 to 223 BCE. In 225 BCE his armies under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xiang-yan">Xiang Yan</a> routed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qin-dynasty">Qin</a> invasion led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/li-xin-qin">Li Xin</a>, but the next year a much larger Qin force under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wang-jian-qin">Wang Jian</a> defeated Chu, and in 223 BCE Fuchu was captured and the kingdom annexed, leaving Qi as the last state to resist Qin.</p></div>
